names an alternative trigger, and gerrit_to_platform.ini.template is not in the recorded 18-path file_impact"],"finding":"The plan's mechanism for making the advisory scanner lane 'present for full-route Gerrit runs' is incomplete: it does not specify how the separate workflow is dispatched per patchset, and the g2p dispatch rule is filename-substring based ('verify' AND 'gerrit'), which the plan neither invokes nor reconciles with its 18-path scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f24d440956edacacd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (\"a separate Gerrit exact-patchset advisory workflow outside gerrit-verify.yaml\") + Testing (\"present for full-route Gerrit runs\") + AC8","norm_id":"n5a422feeb98b4778","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A full-route patchset is created; g2p only auto-dispatches workflows whose filename matches 'verify'+'gerrit'. If the advisory workflow's filename does not match, it is never dispatched per patchset and is NOT 'present for full-route Gerrit runs' — the AC8/Testing held-out contract cannot hold at runtime.","If the filename IS made to match the filter to secure per-patchset presence, that decision (and any dispatch-config change) must be captured, or the static test proving 'present for full-route runs' asserts a property the dispatch layer does not deliver."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Realign parent epic 78f2 AC [RP14/T07] to ADR 0114's advisory-first staging (e.g., 'pinned scanners run in a portable direct-binary parallel ADVISORY lane, promoted into the Verified aggregate only by a later change after a green main run') so the leaf's advisory-only, outside-the-aggregate scope is a consistent subset of the parent contract rather than a contradiction of it.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent 78f2 AC: '[RP14/T07] Pinned deployed Semgrep and Gitleaks integrations run in a portable direct-binary parallel Verified lane.'","Leaf: 'The recreated Gerrit scanner lane must be advisory only and must live outside .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml … It must not be listed in the vote job's needs … Do not promote scanner integration into the voting path in this change.'","ADR 0114 (advisory-first staging) is the leaf's authority but is not referenced anywhere in the parent's plan; the parent AC still literally reads 'Verified lane.'","The leaf's own prior plan-review advisory recorded the needed realignment: 'Realign parent epic 78f2 AC [RP14/T07] to ADR 0114's advisory-first staging …' — yet the parent AC text was never updated.","Per the G7 CONFLICT RULE the parent is authoritative; the productive resolution is to update the parent AC first (staling its plan-review attestation) so the leaf's advisory-only scope becomes a clean subset."],"finding":"The leaf redefines the parent's [RP14/T07] deliverable: the parent AC requires the pinned Semgrep/Gitleaks integrations to 'run in a portable direct-binary parallel Verified lane,' but the leaf delivers an advisory, non-voting scanner lane held OUTSIDE the Verified aggregate (outside gerrit-verify.yaml vote.needs, not in the vote normalization, not in the Verified route decision) and explicitly defers promotion into the voting path to a future change. The parent AC as written still says 'Verified lane' and does not reference ADR 0114, so the leaf's advisory-only disposition contradicts the parent's acceptance criterion rather than narrowing it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbd7676501193ec6e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Leaf aa9e Scope / 'Advisory wiring constraint' / AC 'The scanner lane is wired as advisory for Gerrit …' vs parent 78f2 AC '[RP14/T07] Pinned deployed Semgrep and Gitleaks integrations run in a portable direct-binary parallel Verified lane.'","norm_id":"n481549e59cb2991a","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer verifying the epic's [RP14/T07] completion checks for a Verified-voting scanner lane and finds only an advisory one, reading it as an unmet parent AC.","A future promotion ticket cannot cite a coherent parent contract because the epic AC (Verified lane) and the landed leaf (advisory lane) disagree."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Update parent 78f2 AC [RP14/T07] to reference ADR 0114 and describe the two-step staging (advisory first, Verified promotion later), then re-review the leaf against the corrected parent AC.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no